infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Pairwise self-join: without vs with WHERE a.id < b.id
  desc Same products self-join on equal name — one operator decides the result
  compares
    - label Without WHERE a.id < b.id
      children
        - label Self-match A–A
          desc every row joins itself, a.id equals b.id
        - label Both orders A–B and B–A
          desc each real pair is counted twice
        - label About 1.4M rows
          desc from a table of only 1,200 dupes
        - label Logic right, dedup missing
          desc the most error-prone join
    - label With WHERE a.id < b.id
      children
        - label Self-matches excluded
          desc an id is never less than itself
        - label One ordering kept
          desc A–B yes, mirror B–A dropped
        - label One row per real pair
          desc the correct deduped result
        - label Use < for unordered pairs
          desc switch to <> only to keep both directions
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
